1.Anonymous classes are without name .

2.in the example we saw without writing the whole Credit class as implementation
we are able to write it during method call so this are called "Anonymous classes".

3.Use cases:-

   3.a When we have to implement an interface without creating
       its implementation class or extending a class without writing
       a separate sub-class of it then we use anonymous inner classes.

   3.b When we have to create an object for one time use only then we use it.
